        "retained": [
          "Replace the jagged O(S*N^2) snake traversal with int64 vertical rolling sums and horizontal window rolls.",
          "Store input in one uninitialized flat row-major int allocation and use buffered integer parsing.",
          "Partition output starts into contiguous halo-equipped bands, reducing worker count when halo work dominates.",
          "Apply SIMD only to independent column updates and the explicit initial-sum reduction; do not annotate the loop-carried horizontal roll."
        ]
      },
      "hypothesis": "A flat separable scan exposes dependency-free vertical updates to SIMD while keeping the true horizontal rolling dependency scalar; halo-aware persistent column bands can use available OpenMP workers safely.",
